# ViPER's shell configuration is system wide, in /etc/zsh/viper.zsh, so that it applies
# to the desktop terminal and any SSH session without depending on a dotfile.
#
# This file exists so that zsh does not run zsh-newuser-install, which otherwise opens a
# blocking configuration menu the first time anyone opens a terminal. Anything added
# here overrides the system settings for this account only.
